# Vauxhall Carlton Mk2 saloon, 1986-1994.
#
# The second Carlton: the front-wheel-drive car on the Omega platform
# shared with Opel, sold from November 1986 and the basis of the Lotus
# Carlton. The name was dropped early in 1994 and the car became the Omega,
# so there is no Carlton Mk3. The saloon is modelled; the estate is not
# separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Carlton
#
# Dimensions 4.687 x 1.772 x 1.445 m, wheelbase 2.730 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a TRUE level side elevation, but of an ESTATE,
# with the front bumper clipped at the frame edge; the saloon rear is taken
# from the other views and the body difference is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: intro November 1986; retires staggered 2000-2003 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-carlton-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-carlton-mk2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-carlton-mk2/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the wheelbase and forward flank are derived from a level
# side photograph of an ESTATE with the front bumper clipped, so the saloon
# roof and rear are taken from the oblique saloon photographs. Trim, lens
# internals and plates are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallCarltonMk2(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1986
intro_month=11
retire_year=2003
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=0,1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=443

